# bat (previews, MANPAGER, `cat`-style paging) uses the terminal's 16 colours
# instead of a fixed RGB theme, so it follows the terminal palette (kitty, and
# through it DMS) like the rest of the terminal. themes/ansi.tmTheme replaces the
# built-in `ansi` once `bat cache --build` has run, see the note in that file.
--theme=ansi
